  "body": "`<select multiple>` should not be used for new websites, pending replacement.\r\n\r\nmodern websites do not use `<select multiple>`, instead opting to emulate its behaviour with pretend text boxes that allow typing and selecting choices from a predefined list. standardizing those would be neat, but `<select multiple>` should also be deprecated. (alternatively - would it be viable to add this behaviour to `<select multiple>`? it doesn't seem particularly viable as it has a direct influence in how JS handles keyboard events, even if semantically it's still a `<select multiple>`.)",
